schema: "0.4"
id: npl-minimal-25-tickets-list
type: image
quality: high

# NoizuPromptLingo — a structured prompt-definition language + MCP toolchain for building reliable AI agents — Tickets List screen.
# Theme tenets: near-monochrome gray canvas, single cool sky-blue accent, pure-gray neutrals (no tint), 6px soft radius, gray hairline borders (never hard rules), mono only for literal IDs.
# Palette: canvas #ffffff, ink #0a0a0b, sky accent #0284c7, hairline #e0e0e0/#bdbdbd, alt #f5f5f5, success #16a34a, warning #d97706, error #dc2626.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    barely-there, precise console UI — calm, quietly authoritative, near-monochrome,
    in the restrained register of Linear / Vercel dashboards (NOT colorful, NOT
    playful, NOT a marketing page). Humanist sans-serif (Inter) throughout, NO serif.
    A single cool sky-blue accent carries interactivity; everything else is pure gray.
    Type and quiet gray hairlines do the hierarchy — no drop shadows at rest, no
    gradients, no glow. Structure is felt, not shouted.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of the Tickets List screen of NoizuPromptLingo, a
    prompt-engineering and MCP agent-building platform.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (three bands): a slim achromatic LEFT NAV RAIL of monochrome line
    icons; a dominant CENTER ticket table on a pure-white canvas; and a RIGHT QUEUE
    ACTIVITY FEED panel (about 300px).

    HEADER BAND: a page title "Tickets" in a 600-weight sans, a muted count, and a
    primary solid sky-blue "New ticket" button (white label, small plus glyph, 6px
    radius) at the right.

    CUSTOM FIELD FILTER BAR: a single row of quiet gray-hairline filter pills with
    small chevrons — "Status", "Type", "Priority", "Assignee", and one custom field —
    with one active filter shown as a soft sky-tinted pill ("Status: Open"), and a
    muted "Clear" text control.

    TICKET TABLE (center, the workhorse): about sixteen dense but comfortable rows with
    quiet gray hairline separators, NOT boxed cards. Columns: ID (a small monospace chip
    in JetBrains Mono, e.g. "NPL-142"), TITLE (a 500-weight line with a muted one-line
    snippet beneath on some rows), TYPE (a quiet gray chip — "Bug", "Task", "Spec"),
    STATUS (a small pill paired with a glyph — "Open" quiet gray, "In review" sky, one
    "Blocked" in muted red, one "Done" in green), PRIORITY (a small caret glyph, one
    amber "High"), ASSIGNEE (a small flat neutral avatar dot + name), and UPDATED
    (muted relative time). One column header carries a 500-weight label with a sort
    caret; one row shows a faint gray hover tone.

    QUEUE ACTIVITY FEED (right): a vertical list under a "Recent activity" label with a
    subtle "Today" divider — each row a small neutral avatar dot + a muted line ("Sofia
    moved NPL-138 to In review", "Marcus commented on NPL-140") + a muted relative
    timestamp, separated by quiet hairlines.

    PALETTE & TYPE: near-monochrome — pure white canvas, whisper-cool near-black ink,
    mid and light pure grays for secondary text and hairlines; one calm cool sky-blue
    as the only chrome accent (the New-ticket button, active filter, focus). Status
    color only where meaningful (green done, sky in-review, muted red blocked, amber
    high), always paired with a glyph, never color alone. Monospace (JetBrains Mono)
    only for ticket IDs; humanist sans-serif (Inter) everywhere else, no serif.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: 6px soft corners on the button, pills, and chips; quiet gray
    hairlines separate rows and the feed; flat tonal surfaces, no resting shadows.

    MOOD: precise, calm, efficient — a work queue you scan for hours; dense but never
    crowded, color spent only where it carries meaning.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches the screen's actual layout and key components as specified"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Palette, typography, radius/shape language match the treatise, not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear visual hierarchy, plausible real-product layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"

tags: [npl-minimal, NoizuPromptLingo, screen-mockup]
